## Vulnerability scanning and exceptions

`mise run scan` fails on **fixable** HIGH and CRITICAL findings (`--ignore-unfixed`). When a finding cannot be fixed yet and the risk is understood, add a time-boxed exception to `.trivyignore`. Each entry needs a reason, an owner and an expiry date:

```text
CVE-2026-12345  # reason: not reachable, we never parse untrusted TAR files; owner: platform-team; expires: 2027-01-31
```

`tools/check_scan_exceptions.py` runs first and fails the scan if any entry lacks these fields or has expired, so exceptions cannot quietly become permanent. Prefer fixing: rebuild with `--pull=newer`, bump the dependency (`uv lock --upgrade-package <name>`), or `copier update` to pick up a newer base digest.

`mise run sbom` writes a CycloneDX SBOM (`sbom.cdx.json`) of the image. CI uploads it as a build artifact.
{%- endif %}

